---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Full-stack developer in Mexico working worldwide: production web apps for institutions, fast websites for small businesses, and security review as a standing habit."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1 class="display" style="max-width:16ch">I build the careful kind of software.</h1>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <p>
          I'm {site.name} — a full-stack developer based in {site.location},
          working with clients worldwide in English and Spanish.
        </p>
        <p>
          My background is production systems for institutions: platforms
          where anonymity, data integrity, and uptime are not nice-to-haves.
          That work taught me habits most projects skip — automated tests on
          every change, written specs before code, security review as a
          standing practice instead of a pre-launch panic.
        </p>
        <p>
          I bring exactly those habits to client work. A small-business
          website doesn't need a thousand tests, but it does need someone who
          checks their own work before calling it done. That's the service:
          you get the engineering discipline of institutional software,
          applied to something that loads in under a second and ranks on
          Google.
        </p>
        <h2>What I work with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React, TypeScript, Astro — static-first whenever possible.</li>
          <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Django, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Redis, Celery.</li>
          <li><strong>Ops:</strong> Docker, AWS (EC2, ECR, SSM), CI/CD pipelines, monitoring.</li>
          <li><strong>Security:</strong> auth/session hardening, and ongoing smart-contract security study.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>How engagements run</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>A written scope: what gets built, when, and for how much.</li>
          <li>Weekly demos on a live preview link — progress you can click, not screenshots.</li>
          <li>Launch with tests, documentation, and monitoring in place.</li>
          <li>Full handover: your repository, your hosting, your accounts.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          If that sounds like how software should be built,
          <a href="/contact/">let's talk</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
